{
  "_comment": [
    "CON1 Step 4 — the deterministic VISUAL QA fixture set.",
    "",
    "One row per shape the Content Factory shell has to compose correctly. It is",
    "a fixture of the BACKEND's answers, never a second source of truth: every",
    "`presentation` here is a strict safe projection of the shape",
    "`quiz.premise_projection.build_presentation` emits for that family, and",
    "every `metadata` is the complete stored blob with its solution fields left",
    "in — exactly as the review endpoint returns it. Nothing in the factory may",
    "read a premise from `metadata`; these rows exist so a regression that does",
    "is visible in a picture.",
    "",
    "Asset paths point at the backend `assets/` tree (served locally for offline",
    "runs), so every icon in a capture is a real file and a missing one shows.",
    "",
    "Coverage — the ten cases Step 4 is measured against:",
    "  vq-01  short 4-option MCQ, no premise",
    "  vq-02  long prompt + long options (the readability worst case)",
    "  vq-03  2-option question (the CTA's option-count case)",
    "  vq-04  item recipe visual (missing_component)",
    "  vq-05  champion + ability cinematic band",
    "  vq-06  combat family band (post-mitigation, two champions)",
    "  vq-07  lifecycle family band (purchase/sell swap, item statuses)",
    "  vq-08  Mastery generated question (review_key + provenance, text-only)",
    "  vq-09  Daily frozen card carrying real frozen media",
    "  vq-10  a long-explanation row, for the explanation state",
    "The reveal and explanation cases are STATES over these rows, captured with",
    "--states question,correct,explanation.",
    "CON1 Step 5: vq-03 was a HAND-AUTHORED row shaped like one of the ~50k legacy stored pro_champion_scope_comparison questions. That population is not the current Pro Play serving architecture -- Pro Play generates on demand (pro_authority.on_demand) and the stored rows carry no `context`, so they can never render the production Pro Play card. vq-03 is now a REAL current specimen emitted by quiz.review_render.resolve_review_item; vq-11 and vq-12 add the team and player anchors. All three payloads are the resolver's own output, copied verbatim, never hand-written. The legacy shape's continued REFUSAL is held by a unit test (presentation.proPlay.test.ts) rather than by a fixture row, because a fixture row that must fail would make every clean run report a failure.",
    "",
    "RR1 pass 1 — three rows added so the RANKED production presentation path is",
    "photographable at all. Every `presentation` below is the VERBATIM output of",
    "ranked_public.presentation_render.presentation_for_question() for that row's",
    "family, run against the canonical tables; none is hand-written.",
    "  vq-14  THE GOLD STANDARD. combat_cooldown -> assets.subject.type",
    "         'combat_cooldown' with champion_splash + ability + slot + level +",
    "         ability_rank + item loadout, and deliberately NO assets.entities and",
    "         NO assets.premise_facts -- their presence would divert the payload to",
    "         a family band (bandProfile checks familyLayout BEFORE cinematic), so",
    "         their absence is part of what this row pins. Selects",
    "         CombatCalculationScenarioCard. This is the control group for every",
    "         later convergence change.",
    "  vq-15  The REAL thin Ranked item payload: subject {type,id,name,icon} and",
    "         nothing else. vq-09 is a DAILY card and is richer than anything",
    "         Ranked emits, so it could not serve as the Item Analysis baseline.",
    "         Selects ItemAnalysisScenarioCard with no cost/stats/components.",
    "  vq-16  A DECLARED-DENIED premise (objective_baron_spawn; see",
    "         quiz/presentation_contract.py premise_denied_reason). The resolver",
    "         returns None, so the row carries no `presentation` at all and the",
    "         surface takes the compact band. The absence is the point: this is a",
    "         correct payload, not a missing one.",
    "RR1 summoner-spell convergence: vq-17 is a RESOLVED summoner-spell subject, copied verbatim from presentation_render, and must draw the shared summoner-spell scenario card on the cinematic band with no cooldown anywhere in the media. vq-18 is its fail-closed twin -- Flash has art on disk and NO canonical summoner_spells row, so the backend emits no presentation at all and the question must render the compact band. Do not 'fix' vq-18 by constructing a path from the spell name; the missing rows are owned by the media workstream."
  ],
